[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-331275"] :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-2)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-2)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =2x-2y \\\\  & =2(1)-2(-2) \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x-3y \\\\  & =2(1)-3(-2) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection/bc0149b2bd65704896b7c4c9e555c565419b1e78b0275a38c3370dc2926d4be6" :answer/id #uuid "1175f720-5926-5741-bddd-56ed0683bac3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-72 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection/79fbd6cbdac978bf426f6558a9df8433a5416dc00a5db6dfa031f9d63a8f9632" :answer/id #uuid "0c05fa17-a7bd-5eb9-9fb3-3da10f1dc5b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection/9f678315432cbe2a1ec4f788a5f1adac45152ce4456bc1ba83b2b1601e330954" :answer/id #uuid "bb4a5583-4d97-5391-be74-6d416b3aa2b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection/994f41b21632dfb8408df29dfc438f487d3b3a618f2ab6e8f085f82aad02d84a" :answer/id #uuid "b904762f-2e4f-5d03-b1da-81d0d07867a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection/1566c7c5e41f769f8a910e015e5d9acd092ba3f0565325f48ba311643be16ade" :answer/id #uuid "bbc03b71-f24f-5a53-b579-263145c9b544" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "929d6b2a-2c11-5699-8c0c-9adf8afbf626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332617/selection/79fbd6cbdac978bf426f6558a9df8433a5416dc00a5db6dfa031f9d63a8f9632" :answer-field/choices ["q-332617/selection/bc0149b2bd65704896b7c4c9e555c565419b1e78b0275a38c3370dc2926d4be6" "q-332617/selection/79fbd6cbdac978bf426f6558a9df8433a5416dc00a5db6dfa031f9d63a8f9632" "q-332617/selection/9f678315432cbe2a1ec4f788a5f1adac45152ce4456bc1ba83b2b1601e330954" "q-332617/selection/994f41b21632dfb8408df29dfc438f487d3b3a618f2ab6e8f085f82aad02d84a" "q-332617/selection/1566c7c5e41f769f8a910e015e5d9acd092ba3f0565325f48ba311643be16ade"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332617" :question/id #uuid "75adf624-a2db-5ea7-93a2-7ef71176d432" :question/math-academy-id "q-332617" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+9[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)(\\frac{2}{3})+0(-36) \\\\ 0\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3})+2(-36)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection/24f78033319177443dd5769d55ae21d6c6a8ed86bc7ec708320832265a389541" :answer/id #uuid "4be24466-905c-5bcc-91ff-62cde7a0b22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection/b04a1403b2b31d4ee98954176945d4bb6ced38889fd12c255bc014bf50b9783d" :answer/id #uuid "bdaffa8f-a2e4-515e-ab66-491b33b6d03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection/c0bb241511534a82ed83bf9f68ac61e0b32368db71a28bd7cf3b67bde4af7283" :answer/id #uuid "5efc6ade-eee3-5f3d-bc17-23323f068098" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection/ebb8e0ae8710c67be8c43e111aafc74ad741d679360a64a20c842a2a0f307d6e" :answer/id #uuid "70049e23-1e46-5e0c-9665-dceb31c06ef3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" :answer/id #uuid "391d2adb-3803-5018-a1bd-d9f50f7aa6a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23f4be33-e40d-5bd5-9f53-a21fa5208ae7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332613/selection/24f78033319177443dd5769d55ae21d6c6a8ed86bc7ec708320832265a389541" :answer-field/choices ["q-332613/selection/24f78033319177443dd5769d55ae21d6c6a8ed86bc7ec708320832265a389541" "q-332613/selection/b04a1403b2b31d4ee98954176945d4bb6ced38889fd12c255bc014bf50b9783d" "q-332613/selection/c0bb241511534a82ed83bf9f68ac61e0b32368db71a28bd7cf3b67bde4af7283" "q-332613/selection/ebb8e0ae8710c67be8c43e111aafc74ad741d679360a64a20c842a2a0f307d6e" "q-332613/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332613" :question/id #uuid "72f0ec83-861a-5c13-a044-bab8e690fabf" :question/math-academy-id "q-332613" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-x(t)+4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(3,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(3,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =-x+4y \\\\  & =-3+4(-1) \\\\  & =-3-4 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x+2y \\\\  & =2(3)+2(-1) \\\\  & =6-2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection/04a2f6db171f982f0106856cb01069771f6eef79ab38c730823b32f38fe444be" :answer/id #uuid "d0530f74-bbb3-5ff9-b480-a101121e7f11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection/89a7b50043145b047ec0b49f3140fd1e1b3e4de0bc9d81a9f50ac0b4c1e9f136" :answer/id #uuid "627e608b-1bba-50a7-89b9-ec48baeb2c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection/b201e3565e9e09c1d7c5c40405cfd164be6d28d64aa978763289a6dc9f7aab7d" :answer/id #uuid "1b140876-3f08-5901-8e58-9078eb5c3f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" :answer/id #uuid "6daf1f6b-4ce7-5c78-9c87-289a97f55167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection/cbd3fe56008473a8ce52ca034b4a5760ee0fafddcceb4a8e31044378034ee854" :answer/id #uuid "4b68b109-b013-5789-bf7c-0751423abe09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b1c731c-32eb-5ca5-be25-a69ce334e19c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332610/selection/04a2f6db171f982f0106856cb01069771f6eef79ab38c730823b32f38fe444be" :answer-field/choices ["q-332610/selection/04a2f6db171f982f0106856cb01069771f6eef79ab38c730823b32f38fe444be" "q-332610/selection/89a7b50043145b047ec0b49f3140fd1e1b3e4de0bc9d81a9f50ac0b4c1e9f136" "q-332610/selection/b201e3565e9e09c1d7c5c40405cfd164be6d28d64aa978763289a6dc9f7aab7d" "q-332610/selection/60eadf18022e36714cee17e0479ab6af66a6361ceef7571ec8305b4e57ee6d8f" "q-332610/selection/cbd3fe56008473a8ce52ca034b4a5760ee0fafddcceb4a8e31044378034ee854"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332610" :question/id #uuid "abd93af3-0e28-559c-8c83-70bb59f81df3" :question/math-academy-id "q-332610" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =5x-y \\\\  & =5(1)-(-1) \\\\  & =5+1 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-x-2y \\\\  & =-1-2(-1) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332610/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332610"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" :answer/id #uuid "517ac832-c2ea-5b80-a99b-ff93c447d0f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection/d3e6151f4716169afedda663dfffe855ee128c71e25c44d6f73b5a13c88ebbf1" :answer/id #uuid "37fddaa6-0114-5043-bb3a-238a651a5000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection/76919fca6d742132594c3bb14adc46af27930a7b58ba875bcf6ab1c5e9220e8c" :answer/id #uuid "c8cdeedc-a8ee-576d-b174-c471f0170ca0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection/1764eee0133e8886bb4da8363fff1f2bdd536909fc20ee2cb46e19063c30a5a3" :answer/id #uuid "b3c3c24b-a716-560c-b9bc-e88b2de226ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection/d0630a7e66d385242e74bc4648a2e877a39fa398145ae24cfa60c6ca68b9a200" :answer/id #uuid "649a67d2-262a-530d-9b76-08d2be6fb6bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4e921e6-3e72-5a53-a80b-0ef58b3269e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332618/selection/d0630a7e66d385242e74bc4648a2e877a39fa398145ae24cfa60c6ca68b9a200" :answer-field/choices ["q-332618/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" "q-332618/selection/d3e6151f4716169afedda663dfffe855ee128c71e25c44d6f73b5a13c88ebbf1" "q-332618/selection/76919fca6d742132594c3bb14adc46af27930a7b58ba875bcf6ab1c5e9220e8c" "q-332618/selection/1764eee0133e8886bb4da8363fff1f2bdd536909fc20ee2cb46e19063c30a5a3" "q-332618/selection/d0630a7e66d385242e74bc4648a2e877a39fa398145ae24cfa60c6ca68b9a200"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332618" :question/id #uuid "c444c1ef-e0bd-56b0-aa59-17369145501f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332618" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+8[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(12)+1(8) \\\\ 0(12)+3(8)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24+8 \\\\ 0+24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332618/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332647/field-1/570cbbc381f83341a867c9b2c248ecbbde4fe92928b4719fb7f3333aa7c824a3" :answer/id #uuid "7216eab4-ddf9-57b0-a71a-3e1e872b1743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332647/field-1/074cc99e43ffc0e9c37c20e81d69058e5260c255b226be029ce8964f68cf5c0c" :answer/id #uuid "49675c56-a3e5-5557-a713-562e60ecdb57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332647/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "09d73696-8fa5-5ac0-a8ae-003067973a8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332647/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer/id #uuid "84231776-ca50-5b7c-a1b9-22837e6aaeb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332647/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "73861665-eb66-5d4a-acd9-7510301b0ade" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-332647/field-1/570cbbc381f83341a867c9b2c248ecbbde4fe92928b4719fb7f3333aa7c824a3" :answer-field/choices ["q-332647/field-1/570cbbc381f83341a867c9b2c248ecbbde4fe92928b4719fb7f3333aa7c824a3" "q-332647/field-1/074cc99e43ffc0e9c37c20e81d69058e5260c255b226be029ce8964f68cf5c0c" "q