\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/59a731b27e2333fef2bfa48e9e61a7075548ddd74782c1fadf1dd98f68ef2a7e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332647/field-1" "q-332647/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332647"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332639/field-1/412793739940b973be2b527fb17aec02d6ca6345201ec8cd477bb75bb5283b50" :answer/id #uuid "b4f0c843-350b-5ed4-8421-d0909d231205" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332639/field-1/570cbbc381f83341a867c9b2c248ecbbde4fe92928b4719fb7f3333aa7c824a3" :answer/id #uuid "0fbe89cb-05a0-5741-8af2-61ad16202a38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332639/field-1/b306ad6a3af7dc043f4c3e03da26a15440a9e9b19389783b2e1203bad6e37573" :answer/id #uuid "769b51f4-1f7c-57cb-b0f1-acd2b0abb4b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332639/fie