}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-5x+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/077f785b498c69dfe131ca766df7bad71600e4c7ac28c5a8013603bc56e3be10.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332661/field-1" "q-332661/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332661"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332634/field-1/074cc99e43ffc0e9c37c20e81d69058e5260c255b226be029ce8964f68cf5c0c" :answer/id #uuid "e0b40cdf-19d1-52ae-9efa-560042647cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332634/field-1/e819017e19dccac106b8bdd7a345917915a57ae6ae3646d73f366105b31b91f7" :answer/id #uuid "2cda35dc-ac33-5452-a4f0-5c2ced073a82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332634/field-1/570cbbc381f83341a867c9b2c248ecbbde4fe92928b4719fb7f3333aa7c824a3" :answer/id #uuid "2f2d989c-3ab6-53a7-91d6-53683ae70c25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/vali