ward to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/3ba48b118f4ed24dcf6866579fae201af0b36252e537ab99ac2b87e08a889e15.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection/fe1112621a5a481cb5ed44cc916f32c106e735023d4eedd750fedb3d21f2475f" :answer/id #uuid "a8e64ec7-9669-5782-b6a7-bf19bf39dd3b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/f128b9d7ed44f4b0e7c40177e7198c0593f6ff9b262fae153ffbfad963d00873.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection/6acf0732fe5480a167f80151c1c651b97c7b6adb897a34688bb9980f5b4eecb2" :answer/id #uuid "c512b8e7-e6b0-5762-8b8c-0173a3582d88" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/7d6d07e888cd0dd55fd37a8a620c8be054eee0e6abc170133a4188667dcc65b4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection/b5e9de0177393239c46f5e41f74cb172c388c7fd20a5423aaf45755e8ae6f77b" :answer/id #uuid "359390e3-02e3-537c-b510-db007ffec135" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/f906ea39089da431a1b86d3e7b8ab68ff7a287f8c4af4c3a5b9c1117eff2b57b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection/49d3d80e5ccfa4e5d972eb52eb1b8ca5f6e7b0cc6ea9cf781b7e5ac9be0e354d" :answer/id #uuid "73dd8763-ce70-5d61-bfd3-d89e95bc849e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/0eff17334f3ca56152140bfefaf10a3169ad34a8b6e1e3322bd7fb03963c2338.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection/99355e1b6fe9007cb2786116defba73645269c78734813bf31c4f7113dfb4a6d" :answer/id #uuid "2ed8a33b-77cd-5e96-94b1-87aab643c5c6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/6e2e7d099ed478a259b241320481c4beacda56cea59adc2c7314636f42e79f3e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5fb33e7c-d1a2-5827-a69b-9b5eb090504a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332932/selection/49d3d80e5ccfa4e5d972eb52eb1b8ca5f6e7b0cc6ea9cf781b7e5ac9be0e354d" :answer-field/choices ["q-332932/selection/fe1112621a5a481cb5ed44cc916f32c106e735023d4eedd750fedb3d21f2475f" "q-332932/selection/6acf0732fe5480a167f80151c1c651b97c7b6adb897a34688bb9980f5b4eecb2" "q-332932/selection/b5e9de0177393239c46f5e41f74cb172c388c7fd20a5423aaf45755e8ae6f77b" "q-332932/selection/49d3d80e5ccfa4e5d972eb52eb1b8ca5f6e7b0cc6ea9cf781b7e5ac9be0e354d" "q-332932/selection/99355e1b6fe9007cb2786116defba73645269c78734813bf31c4f7113dfb4a6d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332932" :question/id #uuid "84ea621b-fdfc-5867-8b7a-a801be667c5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332932" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/83147b64f8f34d43b9503186f3d2df5926ce119953c80d10f4cd8b8ef94bfcfc.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, going along with the flow (upward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/6d897c2e9249447cc2d0c902a592d04442b0928c315163b6ab80cff288c84657.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues going upward but then starts turning  to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/bed6896ecc0edcdb157b648108d403e1b8e29463d9f61aa0e0c26e8f5e2dd8c6.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues upward and slightly to the left, suggesting that it may converge to the origin\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/cc53577a278595e5f0155119aa5eb1a7b27ec01847a6daa1ba6ade6792c5f5e9.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332932/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129bee33-7c18-5450-affe-dd710a3a75dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332932"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21585"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/d8be54eddd0358742170a03b3c55e0cb94eaf2a7d59f12e1c4361a6197d29847.png)\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\ln 2?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21586"] :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which $x' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n3x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = 3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which $y' = 0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-2x-y=0 \n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\ny = -2x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/66cdd05ac68d762c5b78df40b22f9e0cd660099c13e48e9eb71c81c73a044280.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21588"] :question/problem "A sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown below (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Sketch the trajectory of the solution starting at the marked point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/0cf7942e618f0465ead5b98c6404a3747e505db75517725971c833c97121ab64.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, moving along with the flow (downward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/105bdbdcac5f0ff20f71a0131bf5bb3cbafe0e93ce8bc733a51c2dcb3fb8364f.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues downward, but the trajectory starts to turn slightly to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/96757a3aee3b161b2ba9887cd85f977f063807779604647dd791cf265790cabc.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues to go downwards and slightly to the left to infinity.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068646/assets/658c15d2291368d0e6836ba19b90157d49dee4a510d58cddf7f85ddc9ff72a8d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
